{"name":"Army Issue","hex":"#8a806b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"army","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, highly organized military force, concerned mainly with ground (rather than air or naval) operations.","Used absolutely for that entire branch of the armed forces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/army"},{"term":"issue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The action or an instance of flowing or coming out, an outflow, particularly:\n A movement of soldiers towards an enemy, a sortie.\n The outflow of a bodily fluid, particularly  in abnormal amounts.","A movement of soldiers towards an enemy, a sortie."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flow out, to proceed from, to come out or from.","To rush out, to sally forth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/issue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Army","blocks":[{"text":"An army, ground force or land force is an armed force that fights primarily on land. In the broadest sense, it is the land-based military branch, service branch, or armed service of a nation or country. It may also include aviation assets by possessing an army aviation component. Within a national military force, the word army may also mean a field army."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/250th_United_States_Army_Birthday_Parade_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_June_14%2C_2025_-_262.jpg/330px-250th_United_States_Army_Birthday_Parade_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_June_14%2C_2025_-_262.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Army","wikidata":"Q37726"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2014%2C_in_New_Delhi_on_January_26%2C_2014.jpg/500px-The_Gorkha_Regiment_marching_contingent_passes_through_the_Rajpath_during_the_65th_Republic_Day_Parade_2